menu "DGX DSI demo"

choice EXAMPLE_BOARD
    prompt "Board"
    default EXAMPLE_BOARD_JC1060P470
    help
        The display, its lanes and its pins. The 10.1-inch board has a chip
        of revision 3: build it with sdkconfig.defaults.jc8012p4a1c, see
        the README.

config EXAMPLE_BOARD_JC1060P470
    bool "Guition JC1060P470: 7-inch 1024x600, JD9165"
    select DGX_ENABLE_JD9165

config EXAMPLE_BOARD_JC8012P4A1C
    bool "Guition JC8012P4A1C: 10.1-inch 800x1280, JD9365"
    select DGX_ENABLE_JD9365

endchoice

config EXAMPLE_LCD_COLOR_BITS
    int "Bits a pixel: 16 or 24"
    default 16
    help
        16 is RGB565: a frame buffer of 1.2 MB. 24 has 256 levels of every
        color and a frame buffer of 1.8 MB; the ramps of the demo show the
        difference.

config EXAMPLE_LCD_TWO_FRAMES
    bool "Two frame buffers: a picture is shown whole, without tearing"
    default n
    help
        With one frame buffer drawing goes into the frame the display is
        reading, and the moving bars of the demo are seen broken now and
        then. With two, a batch of drawing is shown whole at a frame
        boundary, for one more frame of PSRAM.

        Without this the numbers measured on the board decide: when
        dgx_dsi_advise() says that one frame buffer will run the display
        short of data, the display gets two anyway. See the README.

endmenu
